<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTANI BOURSE CLOSED ON 50TH INDEPENDENCE DAY.</title>
<headline>PAKISTANI BOURSE CLOSED ON 50TH INDEPENDENCE DAY.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange was closed on Thursday as Pakistan celebrated its 50th independence anniversary. It will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>The 100-share index closed 31.54 points, or 1.63 percent, down at 1,898.27 amid 157 losers and 59 gainers on Wednesday.</p>
<p>						   Wednesday   August 13</p>
<p>KSE all-share index			  1,232.54    1,247.70</p>
<p>Market capitalisation in billion rupees  579.09	586.22</p>
<p>Trading value in billion rupees		2.06	  2.97</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees)</p>
